   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the military law, in relation to age requirements applicable\nto appointments or promotions of public employees in cities with a population\nof one million or more who have been absent on military duty",
    "basePrintNo": "S6474",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6474-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §243, Mil L",
    "lawSection": "Military Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6474\n\nSPONSOR: GOUNARDES\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the military law, in relation to age\nrequirements applicable to appointments or promotions of public employ-\nees in cities with a population of one million or more who have been\nabsent on military duty\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill would amend subdivision 10-a of § 243 of the Military Law to\nincrease by one year the number of years of military service than can be\ndeducted from the age of an applicant for appointments or promotions to\npositions in public service in a city of one million or more where maxi-\nmum age requirements are established by law, rule or action of the\nmunicipal civil service commission.\n\nSection 243(10-a) of the Military Law currently provides that for public\nservice positions that have a maximum age requirement established by\nlaw, the period of an applicant's military service shall not be included\nin computing the age of the applicant for the purpose of appointment or\npromotion, provided that the total time deducted from the applicant's\nage shall not exceed six years.\n\nSection 1 of the bill would amend subdivision 10-a to provide that in a\ncity with a population of one million or more the total time deducted\nfrom an applicant's age will be increased from six years to seven years.\n\nSection 2 of the bill provides that the act will take effect immediately\nupon enactment.\n\n \nREASONS FOR SUPPORT:\n\nSection 243 of the Military Law provides comprehensive accommodations to\nmilitary veterans who wish to follow their service to the country with\npublic service to New York. For example, it provides veterans who have\nmissed an opportunity to take a civil service examination because of\nservice the right to take a make-up examination.  Similarly, it provides\nto a veteran who passed an examination but missed an opportunity to be\nappointed because of military service to be reinstated to a civil\nservice eligible list and appointed or promoted to a title with retroac-\ntive seniority.\n\nSubdivision 10-a ensures that when the law sets a maximum age limitation\nfor appointment or promotion to a public service position, a veteran's\nyears in military service do not deprive the veteran of the opportunity\nto qualify for service. By excluding from consideration his or her years\nof military service from the computation of the veteran's age, it allows\na veteran whose actual age exceeds the maximum to be considered for\nappointment or promotion.\n\nTwo maximum age limitations have significance for veterans who seek\ntofollow their military careers with service to the City of New York.\nSection 15-103 of the Administrative Code provides that proqualification\nto be a member of the New York City Fire Department a candidate shall\nnot have reached its twenty-ninth birthday at the time he or she applies\nfor a civil service examination. The City of New York has found that\nmilitary veterans are especially well-prepared by experience, training,\nphysical fitness and discipline to perform the duties of members of\nparamilitary organizations such as the FDNY. Enactment of this bill to\nincrease the age limitation for military veterans by one year will\nexpand the pool of highly-prepared individuals while ensuring that\ncandidates who have honorably served our country will be able to contin-\nue to provide public service.\n\nAccordingly, the Mayor urges the earliest possible favorable consider-\nation of this proposal by the Legislature.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
